Input: lm8323 - device tree support; N810 keyboard and touchscreen

The LM8323 keypad controller only took platform data, which no board
provides any more: the Nokia N810's slide-out keyboard had no driver
binding. Without platform data the driver now reads firmware properties:
"linux,keymap" (the chip reports a key as (x << 4) | y, so row x, column
y), the matrix size wired to the chip ("keypad,num-rows" = x,
"keypad,num-columns" = y), "debounce-delay-ms",
"national,active-time-ms", "autorepeat", "label", and the LED class
names of its PWM outputs ("national,pwm-names"). Compatible
"national,lm8323".

N810 DT, after Nokia's board-n800 (via OpenWrt's 3.1 board-n8x0.c):
- the LM8323 on I2C2 (0x45, gpio109), its keymap, and its PWMs as
  Maemo's "keyboard" and "cover" LEDs;
- the TSC2005 touchscreen on McSPI1 CS0 (6 MHz, gpio106, reset gpio94),
  with the LS041Y3 panel's plate resistance and ranges.

